# Atlassian (read-only)

Use `python3 data/changes/tools/atlassian/atl.py` — subcommands `jira issue|search|links|comments|xml` and
`confluence search|page|diff`. Credentials in `~/.config/<org>/jira.env` (each person's own token; never commit or
print it). The tool only sends GET. Jira writes stay with the human; a Confluence page update goes through
`confluence_write.py` (plan → diff → explicit human OK for that page → apply) and only when the human asks for it.
A ticket status table refreshed from Jira is report-only unless this machine is the publisher per
`data/changes/s3-sync/IDENTITY.md`.

Full procedure (setup, exit codes, examples): `.cursor/skills/atlassian/SKILL.md`. Collecting service-run evidence
(source, generated artefact, result JSON, logs) is a different tool: `.cursor/skills/evidence/SKILL.md`.
